        "original_id": "5c755975-b703-51a9-a5cf-39ee08b57ec3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: sirenian evolution, fossil record\n- Animals: sirenians, dugong, manatees, Sirenia\n\nFacts:\n- Sirenians are thought to have a fossil record spanning about 50 million years from the early Eocene to the present.\n- The order Sirenia has four living species, including the dugong and three species of manatees.\n- The dugong is the only strictly marine herbivorous mammal.",
